Now part 5: AI + fx + final missing methods.

AI implementation details:

```js
runAI(dt) {
  for (const team of this.teams) {
    team.aiTimer -= dt;
    team.aiPassCd = Math.max(0, team.aiPassCd - dt);
    team.aiKickCd = Math.max(0, team.aiKickCd - dt);
  }
  const b = this.ball;
  const attacking = b.owner ? b.owner.team : (b.state === 'pass' && b.passFrom ? b.passFrom.team : null);

  for (const team of this.teams) {
    for (const p of team.players) {
      if (p.state !== 'run' || p.scripted) continue;
      if (team.isUser && p === this.controlled && !this.isUserPossessionJump?) skip always for user control.
      if (b.state === 'held' && b.owner) {
        if (team === b.owner.team) {
          if (p === b.owner) { if (!(team.isUser && p===this.controlled)) this.aiCarry(p, dt); }
          else this.aiSupport(p, dt);
        } else {
          this.aiDefend(p, dt);
        }
      } else if (b.state === 'pass') {
        if (attacking && team === attacking && p !== (b.target||{})) this.aiSupport(p, dt);
        else if (team === attacking) this.aiSupport? For target, aiChase? 
        else this.aiChase(p, dt, true);
      } else {
        this.aiChase(p, dt);
      }
    }
  }
}
```
- For user-controlled player, skip AI entirely (handleUserInput set movement).
- On defense with ball held, user's controlled skips; teammates AI defend.
- If ball owner is user and controlled, skip aiCarry.

But if team.isUser and possession, support uses AI; good.

AI refresh roles in `aiDefend`:
```
if (team.aiTimer <= 0) {
 team.aiTimer = 0.35;
 const threat = b.owner? b.owner : {x:b.x,y:b.y};
 const sorted = team.players.filter(p=>p.state==='run' || p.state==='dive').slice().sort((a,b)=>dist2(a,threat)-...);
 team.defRoles.clear();
 sorted.forEach((p,i)=> team.defRoles.set(p.id, i<2?'chase':'line'));
 const linePlayers = team.players.filter(p=>team.defRoles.get(p.id)==='line').sort((a,b)=>a.y-b.y);
 linePlayers.forEach((p,i)=> p.defSlot = i - (linePlayers.length-1)/2);
}
```

Careful team.aiTimer is shared and decremented in runAI for both teams every frame; good. But `aiDefend` recompute inside for first player only? Since aiTimer <=0 for all players, the first player's aiDefend recomputes and sets aiTimer, subsequent see >0. Good.

`aiDefend(p, dt)`:
```
const b=this.ball;
const team=p.team;
const carrier = b.owner && b.owner.team!==team ? b.owner : null;
const threat = carrier || {x:b.x,y:b.y, vx:b.vx||0, vy:b.vy||0};
const role = team.defRoles.get(p.id) || 'line';
if (role==='chase') {
  const tx = threat.x + (threat.vx||0)*0.22;
  const ty = threat.y + (threat.vy||0)*0.22;
  const d = dist(p.x,p.y,tx,ty);
  let dx = tx-p.x, dy=ty-p.y;
  // if very close, dive
  if (carrier && d < 2.2 && p.tackleCd<=0) { this.startDive(p); return; }
  // avoid overlap
  set movement normalized; sprint if d>3
} else {
  const def = team.defenseStyle;
  const ownLine = team.dir>0 ? 0 : 100;
  let tx = b.x - team.dir*def.depth;
  // rush
  tx += team.dir * def.rush * 3.2;
  // keep between own line and ball
  const minX = Math.min(ownLine+4, b.x + team.dir*2);...
  targetY = clamp(b.y + (p.defSlot||0)*10.5, 6, 64);
  // drift: follow ball y
  targetY = lerp(targetY, b.y, def.drift*0.25)
  movement; sprint if far>8
  // if carrier within 1.4 passive handled
  if (carrier && dist<2.0 && p.tackleCd<=0 && (def.aggression>0.8 || Math.random()<0.02)) startDive
}
```
Hmm defenders behind the ball? `tx = b.x - team.dir*def.depth`:
- Team dir +1 (attacking right, defending own left try line at 0). Defenders should be to the left of the ball → b.x - depth. Yes.
- Opponent with dir -1 (attacks left, defends right line 100). Defenders should be to the right of ball → b.x - (-1)*depth = b.x + depth. Yes.
- So correct.

`defSlot` line spread: linePlayers sorted by y; offset index centered. Spacing 10.5 * width? Defense has no width. Use 11.

Avoid clustering with chasers: role chase 2 players.

AI chaser should approach from the inside (toward own try line) to force sideways? Keep direct.

`aiChase(p, dt)`:
```
let tx, ty;
if (b.state==='kick') { const pred=this.predictLanding(); tx=pred.x; ty=pred.y; }
else { tx=b.x + b.vx*0.18; ty=b.y + b.vy*0.18; }
// assign only some players to chase? All chasing leads to swarm; better: nearest 3 per team. Compute each frame roles
```
For loose ball, all 7 chasing looks chaotic. Let's compute `team.chaseRoles` similarly, with nearest 3. But aiChase is called for all. Add inside:
```
if (team.aiChaseTimer <= 0) { compute list of 3 nearest by dist to ball; team.chaseSet = new Set(ids) }
if (!team.chaseSet.has(p.id)) { hold position: move to a support/covering position }
```
- Simpler: let all chase but apply a "support offset" to non-chasers. To keep it quick, allow all to chase but limit speed for far players? Visually okay. But you'd have 14 players converging. Let's do nearest 3 chase, others cover:
  - Each team: `team.aiChaseTimer` decrement; every 0.4s compute sorted by distance; 3 chasers; store IDs.
  - Non-chasers: position behind ball (team.isUser? support) or spread; use a point ball.x - dir*8, ball.y + offset; but if it's a kick, backs should retreat.
  - Implement in aiChase: if not a chaser → target = (ball.x - team.dir*10, ball.y + slot*8), clamp; move slowly.

- Keep chasers sprint.
- For the user team, controlled may not be in chaseSet but user moves them.

`aiCarry`:
```
const team=p.team, dir=team.dir, b=this.ball;
const goalX = dir>0?100:0;
const tryLine=goalX;
const nearestOpp=nearestOf(other.players,...)
const pressure=...
// base direction
let dx = goalX - p.x; let dy = 35 - p.y;
// prefer gaps: find defenders within 12 ahead; steer away laterally
for opp within 10: 
  const ox = opp.x-p.x, oy=opp.y-p.y;
  const ahead = ox*dir > -2;
  if ahead: const w = (1 - Math.hypot(ox,oy)/12); dx -= (ox/ d)*w*0.3? Actually push away from defender in y:
  dy += (p.y - opp.y > 0 ? 1 : -1) * w * 2.5
```
Better use repulsion:
```
let fx = dir*1.0, fy = (35-p.y)*0.012;
for opp:
  const ddx=p.x-opp.x, ddy=p.y-opp.y; d=...
