content.text:
Mobile now players bigger (about 40px? screenshot 2x shows ~50px). Good. But there is a problem: the camera on mobile is zoomed such that the player card + touch controls cover the bottom 40%; and the controlled player (yellow ring) appears at upper third. That's because camera focus is ball/controlled at y 40.7, and the screen is tall. Fine.

However, in mobile screenshot, the kickoff ball is loose at right? "Kick-off!" commentary, ball at x? The controlled player has ring; ball elsewhere? The white/black ball on right at x~730. It's after kick, loose. Fine.

Desktop zoom is good: players 32px, visible ~58x36. The pitch lines and space look better.

Wait desktop screenshot: ball is at far right, loose, with landing indicator dashed circle. The user controlled yellow ring. Good.

Camera bug: On mobile, camera x 61.4 while ball at ~? It followed kick landing. Fine.

Now a significant issue: the mobile HUD has the player card at bottom 232px and touch controls below; the ball/action area around y 560. Fine.

The mobile portrait still shows a lot of vertical pitch (60 units), but that's okay.

Now, the conversion camera: with portrait max scale 14, *1.16 = 16.3, visible width 24, height 52. Should be okay.

Next, test the custom play execution visually, maybe ensure formation routes drawn. We tested auto pass. Good.

Now fix the play editor name input mobile layout by adding a media rule. Not crucial but polish. Add at <=560:
```
.play-editor-head { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
.play-editor-actions { width: 100%; }
.play-editor-actions .btn { flex:1; }
.play-name-input { font-size: 20px; }
```
Also the "New" button etc.

Then README. But before, inspect git/diff? All untracked, no baseline. Fine.

Let's consider additional core gameplay issue: The user cannot score easily because the match camera/scene but controls fine. Let's play a manual-ish session and try to score using direct input to ensure try & conversion UI work from real input. Our qa3 teleported and scored, so mechanism okay.

Maybe test one real try via bot: set match clock etc. Hard.

Let's test `triggerPlay` via key in real loop after obtaining possession:
- Start match; skip kickoff via kickoffKick; set user possession with player at 40; press Digit1; see activePlay; after 1s pass; screenshot. This validates keyboard path and UI banner. We already direct-called triggerPlay; need input path. Let's run a focused test and capture.

Also test touch tactic button path (data-tactic). Useevaluate pointerdown? The touch buttons have own listener adding edge; engine reads in main loop. We can click with page.touchscreen.tap on `[data-tactic="1"]`; but these are only visible in touch mode. Test with mobile after possession. Might be worthwhile.

Also potential bug: input.bindTouch called once in constructor; `bindHudPlays()` later re-renders `touch-tactics` innerHTML, destroying old buttons and their event listeners! The `bindTouch` attaches listeners to `#touch-tactics` children at construction, but `bindHudPlays` replaces them when entering match and when equipping. So touch tactic buttons lose their direct listeners. However, `bindTouch` tacticRoot attaches listeners to each button; new buttons have none. Yet `input.bindTouch` also adds an edge if onTactic; but no listener. So touch tactics may be broken! Wait `bindHudPlays` re-renders and there might be event delegation? No. `bindTouch` only attaches to existing at time of constructor. On enterMatch, bindHudPlays rebuilds touch tactics. Therefore touch tactic buttons do nothing. That's a real bug.

Similarly `.touch-actions` buttons are static, fine. `.touch-tactics` is dynamic. Need fix: use event delegation on the `#touch-tactics` root in input.bindTouch, so it works after re-render. Or call bindTouch again after render (would duplicate stick listeners, bad). Better modify bindTouch:
```
if (tacticRoot) {
  tacticRoot.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e)=>{
    const b = e.target.closest('[data-tactic]');
    if (!b) return;
    const i = Number(b.dataset.tactic);
    e.preventDefault();
    this.edges.add(`tactic${i}`);
    onTactic?.(i-1);
  });
}
```
This root listener persists across innerHTML changes. Also prevent duplicate binding: bindTouch called once. Good.

Let's fix. Also note `onTactic` passed null; engine reads edge, fine. Could pass a direct triggerPlay callback for responsiveness, but edge is processed next frame. Good.

Also touch "KICK" press/release listeners are static button root, unaffected. Good.

Let's patch input.js.

